      "nodes": "caption",
      "lines": "2",
      "reason": "`![a][nope]` + `^ cap` is one paragraph: the reference does not resolve, so the image is literal text and the `^` line is literal with it. Whether it resolves depends on the DEFINITIONS in the document, which a context-free grammar does not have - so the caption is built here and cannot be declined without a symbol table. The renderer decides correctly; highlighting a caption that the language declines is the cost."
    }
